        "timestamp": 1780911248,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Peruvians await results of elections for ninth president in a decade Americas Issued on: 08/06/2026 - 11:34 The presidential election in Peru to determine the 9th head of state in a decade is too close to call. Right-wing candidate, Keiko Fujimori ran on promises to be tough on crime and is the daughter of the late, former president and authoritarian figure Alberto Fujimori who was convicted of human rights abuses. Left-wing candidate Roberto Sanchez, an ally of jailed former president Pedro Castillo, has vowed to address the socioeconomic divide between those living in cities and rural areas. The winner will likely be declared in some days after a full count is completed. Iran heads to World Cup in Mexico amid bitter visa standoff with Washington 07/06/2026 Americas Bolivian police clash with protesters demanding president's resignation 07/06/2026 Americas Peru votes for its ninth president in 10 years 07/06/2026 Americas 'Deplorable issues' cloud 2026 FIFA World Cup, deemed 'one of the least anticipated of this era' 04/06/2026 Sport 2026 World Cup: National teams begin to arrive in North America 04/06/2026 Sport US finds huge tunnel on the Mexican border used to smuggle drugs 03/06/2026 Americas Wembanyama chases NBA dream ahead of Spurs-Nicks final 03/06/2026 Americas As California votes in the primary elections, who are the candidates? 03/06/2026 Americas Californian elections test for divided Democrats on pivotal primary election day 03/06/2026 Americas"
